# CHAPTER IV

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

#### Article 16

The Implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence is a joint obligation and responsibility of:  
a. Regional Government;  
b. Private Sector and Community Institutions;  
c. Community; and  
d. Family and/or Parents.

#### Article 17

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 16 letter a include:  
a. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
b. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;  
c. conducting cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, as well as educational institutions, health institutions, hospitals, and various non-governmental organizations concerned with women and children from acts of violence;  
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children, in accordance with regional financial capacity;  
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children; and  
g. realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.  
2. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and victim protection action activities in the Regional Action Plan and Main Performance Indicators in supporting the main regional programs as a basis for the Region in implementing the protection of women and children.  
3. The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), is part of the RPJMD.  
4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan (4) as referred to in paragraph (2) are regulated by Regent's Decree.

#### Article 18

The Regent in carrying out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in Article 17 delegates to the relevant Regional Apparatus/Institutions.

#### Article 19

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Private Sector and Community Institutions as well as the Community as referred to in Article 16 letter b, letter c, are implemented in the form of community participation.  
2. The form of community participation as referred to @) in paragraph (1), includes:   
a. preventing the occurrence of violence against women and children;  
b. providing emergency assistance to victims;  
c. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties;  
d. protecting victims; and €. participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence;  
3. The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), is carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 20

The Obligations of Family and/or Parents as referred to in Article 16 letter d, who legally have full responsibility to prevent all forms of violence and protect women and children as Family members.

# CHAPTER V

## IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION

## Part One

Institutional

#### Article 21

1. The Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and the community.  
2. Empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by:  
a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;  
b. providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;  
c. creating a friendly and safe work environment atmosphere for women;  
d. building community participation and concern for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
e. building and providing an information system that is easily accessible;  
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; and  
g. providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.

#### Article 22

1. In order to implement services and protection for women and children from acts of violence.  
2. The Regional Government establishes UPTD PPA UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1), functions to implement services:  
a. public complaints;  
b. victim outreach;  
c. case management;  
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and  
f. victim assistance.

#### Article 23

1. In implementing protection for women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government may also establish a task force.  
2. The task force as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:  
a. Task Force for the Prevention and Handling of Criminal Acts of Human Trafficking;  
b. Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children;  
c. Task Force for the Prevention of Child Marriage;
3. Further provisions regarding the position, organizational structure, duties and functions as well as working procedures of the task force as referred to in paragraph (2) are stipulated by Regent's Regulation.

#### Article 24

The Regional Government may establish KPAD in the supervision of the implementation of child protection in the region.  Further provisions regarding the position, organizational structure, duties and functions as well as working procedures of KPAD are regulated by Regent's Regulation.

#### Article 25

1. The Regional Government may establish Satgas PPA in an effort to coordinate the implementation of services for Women and Children victims of acts of violence.  
2. Satgas PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) aims to:  
a. coordinate and synchronize protection services for women and children carried out by the Regional Government, Regional Apparatus/Institutions and the community;  
b. improve cooperation and referral systems; and
c. collect, compile and present reports of violence.  
3. The establishment of Satgas PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) is stipulated by Regent's Decree.

#### Article 26

1. Village Government and/or Lurah as representatives of the Regional Government in the implementation of child protection at the village/kelurahan level may establish PATBM.  
2. PATBM functions as a network or community group that works in a coordinated manner in the implementation of child protection at the village/kelurahan level.  
3. The establishment of PATBM as referred to in paragraph (1) is stipulated by Village Head's Decree.

## Part Two

Prevention

#### Article 27

1. Efforts to prevent violence against Women and Children are carried out in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:  
a. PPPA;  
b. social affairs;  
c. health;  
d. education;  
e. manpower;  
f. population and civil registration;  
g. law;  
g. cooperatives and micro enterprises;  mental and spiritual; and  peace and order.  
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. building cooperation with law enforcement apparatus;  
b. law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, as well as Educational Institutions, Health institutions, hospitals, various NGOs concerned with women and children;  
c. building community and family participation and concern for the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;  establishing a violence prevention system that provides a complete and easily accessible information system;  
d. conducting socialization on laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence;  
e. providing critical education on the rights of women and children as victims of violence to the community; and  
f. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.  
3. Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

## Part Three

Forms and Service Mechanisms

text:
#### Pasal 28

Bentuk pelayanan terhadap tindak kekerasan yang dialami  (1) oleh Perempuan dan Anak meliputi:  
a. pelayanan pengaduan;  
b. pelayanan kesehatan;  
c. bantuan hukum;  
d. penyampaian laporan;  
e. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial,  rehabilitasi, dan pelayanan pendampingan.  
2. Dalam melaksanakan bentuk pelayanan sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (1) Pemerintah Daerah bekerjasama  dengan perangkat daerah/lembaga terkait.

#### Pasal 29

Pelayanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 28  ayat (1) huruf a, meliputi:  
a. identifikasi atau pencatatan awal korban; dan  
b. persetujuan dilakukan tindakan (informed consent).

#### Pasal 30

Pelayanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 28  ayat (1) huruf b, meliputi:  
a. pertolongan pertama kepada korban;  
b. perawatan dan pemulihan luka-luka fisik yang bertujuan  untuk pemulihan kondisi fisik korban yang dilakukan  oleh tenaga medis dan paramedik; dan  
c. rujukan ke layanan kesehatan.  
d. medicolegal;  

pendampingan psikologis.

#### Pasal 31

1. Pelayanan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 28 ayat (1) huruf c, bertujuan membantu korban  dalam menjalani proses peradilan.  
2. Pelayanan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) dilakukan dengan cara:  
a. memberikan konsultasi hukum yang mencakup  informasi mengenai hak korban dan proses peradilan;  
b. mendampingi korban di tingkat pelaporan, penyidikan,  penuntutan, dan pemeriksaan dalam sidang  pengadilan dan membantu korban untuk secara  lengkap memaparkan kekerasan yang dialaminya; dan  
c. melakukan koordinasi dengan sesama penegak  hukum, relawan pendamping, dan pekerja sosial agar  proses peradilan berjalan sebagaimana mestinya.

#### Pasal 32

Pelayanan penyampaian laporan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 28 ayat (1) huruf d, bertujuan mendampingi perempuan  dan anak sebagai korban tindak kekerasan setelah diperoleh  hasil mediasi dari UPTD PPA.

#### Pasal 33

1. Pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 28 ayat (1) huruf e, bertujuan untuk  mengembalikan korban untuk diterima kembali dalam  lingkungan sosialnya.  
2. Pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial korban sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan setelah  sosialisasi terkait hak-hak perempuan dan anak sebagai  korban kekerasan.  
3. Pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (2) dilakukan oleh Pemerintah Daerah  berkoordinasi dengan perangkat daerah/lembaga terkait,  dan masyarakat.

#### Pasal 34

1. Pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 28 ayat (1) huruf f, meliputi:  
a. motivasi dan diagnosis psikososial;  
b. bantuan dan asistensi sosial;  
c. perawatan dan pengasuhan;  
d. pelatihan vokasional dan pembinaan kewirausahaan;
e. bimbingan mental spiritual;  
f. bimbingan fisik;  
g. bimbingan sosial dan konseling psikososial;  
h. pelayanan aksesibilitas;  
i. bimbingan resosialisasi;  
j. bimbingan lanjut; dan/atau  
k. rujukan.  
2. Bentuk pelatihan vokasional dan pembinaan  kewirausahaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) huruf c, meliputi:  
a. pelatihan keterampilan;  
b. praktek kerja lapangan;  
c. pemagangan;  
d. pelatihan keterampilan wirausaha;  
e. fasilitasi pembentukan kelompok usaha bersama;  
f. modal usaha berupa alat penunjang usaha; dan  
g. pendampingan pelaksanaan usaha.

#### Pasal 35

Pelayanan Pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal  28 ayat (1) huruf g, meliputi:  
a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan  pemulihan kesehatan;  
mendampingi korban selama proses medicolegal;  
b. mendampingi korban selama proses mediasi dan/atau  pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan, dan Pengadilan;  memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses  pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;  
c. menjaga privasi dan kerahasiaan korba dari semua pihak  yang tidak berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh  media massa;  
d. melakukan koordinasi dengan pendamping yang lain; dan  memberikan penanganan yang berkelanjutan hingga  tahap rehabilitasi.

#### Pasal 36

1. Penyelenggaraan pelayanan terhadap Korban sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 28 dilaksanakan setiap hari  (termasuk hari libur), secara:  
a. cepat;  
b. aman dan nyaman;  
c. rasa empati;  
d. non diskriminasi;  
e. mudah dijangkau;  
f. tidak dikenakan biaya; dan  
g. dijamin kerahasiaannya.  
2. Penyelenggara atau pengelola pelayanan dilarang  memungut biaya apapun terhadap korban kekerasan.

## Bagian Keempat

Pendampingan

#### Pasal 37

1. Pemerintah Daerah dapat melakukan pendampingan  terhadap perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan.  
2. Pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),  meliputi seluruh upaya yang terpadu untuk memulihkan  dan menguatkan kondisi korban, yang dilakukan di unit  layanan kesehatan, pendidikan, kepolisian, kejaksaan,  pengadilan, dan lembaga layanan sosial.  
3. Pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2),  dilakukan oleh pendamping UPTD PPA dan Pendamping  lainnya.

# BAB VI

## PELINDUNGAN KHUSUS ANAK

#### Pasal 38

1. Pemerintah Daerah dan lembaga lainnya berkewajiban dan  bertanggung jawab untuk memberikan Perlindungan  Khusus kepada Anak.  
2. Pelindungan Khusus kepada Anak sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1), diberikan kepada:  
a. Anak dalam Situasi Darurat;  
b. Anak yang Berhadapan dengan Hukum;  
c. Anak dari Kelompok Minoritas dan Terisolasi;  
d. Anak yang Dieksploitasi secara Ekonomi dan/atau  Seksual;  
e. Anak yang menjadi Korban Penyalahgunaan  Narkotika, Alkohol, Psikotropika, dan Zat Adiktif  lainnya,  
f. Anak yang Menjadi Korban Pornografi;  
g. Anak dengan HIV dan AIDS;  
h. Anak Korban Penculikan, Penjualan, dan/atau Perdagangan;  
i. Anak Korban Kekerasan Fisik dan/atau Psikis;  
j. Anak Penyandang Disabilitas, Anak Korban Kejahatan Seksual;  
k. Anak Korban Jaringan Terorisme;  
l. Anak yang Menjadi Korban Stigmatisasi dari Pelabelan;  
m. Anak Korban Perlakuan Salah dan Penelantaran;  
n. Anak dengan Perilaku Sosial Menyimpang, dan Terkait dengan Kondisi Orang Tuanya.  
3. Pelindungan Khusus bagi Anak dilakukan melalui upaya:  
a. penanganan yang cepat, termasuk pengobatan  dan/atau rehabilitasi secara fisik, psikis, dan sosial,  serta pencegahan penyakit dan gangguan kesehatan  lainnya;  
b. pendampingan psikososial pada saat pengobatan  sampai pemulihan;  
c. pemberian bantuan sosial bagi Anak yang berasal dari  keluarga tidak mampu; dan  
d. pemberian pelindungan dan pendampingan pada  setiap proses peradilan.  
4. Pelindungan Khusus Kepada Anak sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) diberikan di UPTD PPA yang telah dibentuk  dengan mengacu kepada standar layanan yang telah  ditetapkan.  
5. Pelindungan Khusus kepada Anak sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan secara cepat, komprehensif dan  terintegrasi.

